// @emit-error an i32-keyed Map/Set is supported as a binding / parameter / return / `| null` only
// CAPABILITY (B6a, i32-keyed half): the POSITIONS an i32-keyed map may occupy.
// It has no mv slot, no ref-list element heap and no struct-field cell of its own
// — those all resolve through the per-VALUE map-struct layer the i32-keyed rep
// does not join — so a LIST of i32-keyed maps is a loud reject. The gate is one
// containment test over every annotation spelling (`collectA`'s `TypeRef` walk),
// so the message names the whole spelling that failed.
//
// The supported set is stated in the message and pinned positively by
// `i32-keyed-scopes.vl`: a binding, a parameter, a return, and `| null`.
const xs: {[i32]: i32}[] = [Map()]
xs[0][1] = 2
print(xs[0].length)
